id: core/agency-interface
title: "purpose-conditioned recursive agency interface"
kind: synthesis-contract
status: proposed-0.1
updated: 2026-09-07
governing_sources:
  - core/motivation-and-purpose.yawn
  - core/world-field-arena.yawn
  - core/orientation.yawn
  - core/inquiry-selection.yawn
  - core/co-orientation-loop.yawn
  - core/movement-loop.yawn
  - core/what-is-a-yawn.yawn
  - core/objective-holon.yawn
  - spec/ontology.md
  - spec/questions.md
  - q-space/protocol-v1.yawn
supporting_research: references/PURPOSE_CONDITIONED_AGENCY_RESEARCH_BRAID.yawn
ontological_status: "names what the governing sources already say; adds no primitive"
epistemic_status: reported
epistemic_note: "a synthesis reported by the principal from an OpenAI model; the alignment claims were checked by the recorder (observed); the extensions marked as such are inferred"
provenance: >
  Supplied by the principal on 2026-09-07 as a research synthesis authored by an
  OpenAI model in his ChatGPT thread (model unrecorded). Recorded by
  agent:anthropic:claude-code. Its claims about this protocol were checked
  against the governing sources above; its claims about outside research are
  reported and carried in the research braid with verification owed. The
  principal's personal material in the source is held privately and is not in
  this repository.

purpose: >
  State, in one place, what the protocol is for, so that apertures, selectors,
  and stewards can be checked against it instead of rediscovering it.

statement: >
  A purpose-conditioned, question-driven, holonic agency system through which a
  human and AI can jointly discover what matters, externalize their current
  model, identify what is missing, pursue warranted action with machine
  leverage, learn from consequences, and recursively improve the process by
  which they orient and act.

levels:
  product: "a holonic reality interface"
  cognitive: "an externalized orientation-and-agency loop"
  ai_systems: "a governed recursive improvement architecture"
  human: >
    a cognitive companion that helps a person move from implicit experience to
    explicit, revisable, actionable understanding without pretending the
    representation is the person or reality

gap_named: >
  Conventional agents begin after the objective has been specified. A person
  often needs intelligence because the objective is not yet known, its reason
  is unclear, it conflicts with something deeper, or one unanswered question
  prevents movement. core/motivation-and-purpose.yawn already lets a desire
  exist without becoming a goal, commitment, authorization, or action. That
  separation is the protocol's answer to the wish-granting problem: the
  interface does not ask "what is your wish"; it supports "here is what I am
  experiencing; help me understand what may matter; show me what you
  inferred and what we do not know; help me choose the clarifying question;
  let me revise the purpose; then give that intention leverage, governed".

four_convergent_ideas:
  - relationship_is_prior: "what is observable, relevant, actionable, and permitted depends on the situated agent–arena relationship (spec/ontology.md)"
  - orientation_precedes_optimization: "observations, desires, tensions, unknowns, relationships, and questions may exist before any goal is promoted (core/motivation-and-purpose.yawn)"
  - questions_expose_missing_structure: "Q-Space keeps attributed answers, candidate questions, probes, transitions, and proof without equating repetition or model output with truth (q-space/protocol-v1.yawn)"
  - consequences_close_the_loop: "reality is whatever constrains consequences and can disconfirm the record; the map must not grow coherent by talking to itself (core/world-field-arena.yawn)"

why_is_not_one_relation:
  rule: "the kinds below may not share one answer; a fluent paragraph that resolves them together is a category error"
  kinds:
    - { id: causal, example: "why did this start?", answerable_by: "evidence and history" }
    - { id: motivational, example: "why do I continue despite the cost?", answerable_by: "reported experience and evidence" }
    - { id: normative, example: "why should I continue?", answerable_by: "ethical reasoning and deliberation" }
    - { id: teleological, example: "what purpose would continuing serve?", answerable_by: "a purpose the principal ratifies" }
    - { id: psychological, example: "what need, value, fear, identity, attachment, or conflict participates in the pull?", answerable_by: "evidence and reflection" }
    - { id: epistemic, example: "why do I believe something important is here?", answerable_by: "evidence, falsifiers, proof" }
    - { id: existential, example: "why am I here at all?", answerable_by: "no current empirical answer; held as a question" }
  consistent_with: "core/orientation.yawn treats intent as one of nine axes; purpose may be chosen, inherited, imposed, requested, or unclear"

purpose_conditioned_question_frontier:
  description: >
    Not a primitive; a description of the interaction. At any moment many
    questions are open. The important one is not necessarily the deepest: it
    is the one whose answer would most change orientation relative to what
    currently matters. Purpose conditions priority without becoming
    unquestionable.
  inputs: [current_orientation, currently_endorsed_purposes, open_lacunae, consequence_or_risk, relationship_and_authority]
  comparator: >
    priority(q, t) ≈ information_gain(q) × relevance(q, purposes_t) × consequence(q)
    × decision_impact(q) ÷ (burden(q) + risk(q) + delay(q))
  hard_gates_in_order: [immediate_safety_or_stability, authority_or_consent_blocker, privacy_visibility_or_egress_blocker, source_or_provenance_loss, proof_or_falsifier_integrity]
  gate_rule: "a gate that is not clear forces a foregrounded hold; no score bypasses it (core/inquiry-selection.yawn)"
  status: "engineering formalization aligned with epistemic/pragmatic value in active inference and with core/inquiry-selection; not a psychological law"
  consequence: >
    the principal does not need to know an ultimate purpose first; a current
    purpose such as "understand why this has such a hold on me and decide
    what, if anything, deserves to happen next" is enough to orient.

holon_as_nine_questions:
  - { id: what_is_here, holds: [observations, reports, people, context, relationships] }
  - { id: what_matters, holds: [desires, values, needs, purposes, commitments] }
  - { id: what_do_we_think, holds: [claims, models, assumptions, perspectives, answers] }
  - { id: what_dont_we_know, holds: [questions, lacunae, disputes, uncertainty] }
  - { id: what_could_happen, holds: [affordances, options, predictions, candidate_moves] }
  - { id: what_may_happen, holds: [authority, consent, privacy, boundaries] }
  - { id: what_happened, holds: [events, consequences, feedback] }
  - { id: what_did_that_teach_us, holds: [proof, revisions, changed_relationships] }
  - { id: what_now, holds: [new_question, movement, hold, delegation] }
  note: "this is core/what-is-a-yawn.yawn read as questions: a bounded orientation contract around something that matters enough to maintain continuity"

steward:
  definition: "a Yawnbot is what happens when a holon is given stewardship; activation stays distinct from authority (spec/ontology.md)"
  may: [notice_relevant_change, retrieve_context, surface_missing_structure, ask_a_discriminating_question, commission_research, compare_perspectives, propose_movement, perform_authorized_work, watch_for_consequences, request_verification, update_the_model, resurface_when_relevant]
  may_not: [invent_the_principals_purpose, convert_inference_into_truth, convert_ability_into_permission, declare_its_own_improvement_successful, treat_disagreement_as_pathology, treat_popularity_as_evidence]

loop:
  stages: [experience, orientation, lacunae, question_frontier, perspective_field, answer_frontier, next_warranted_turn, principal_choice, leverage, consequence_and_proof, model_update, purpose_update, next_orientation]
  purpose_position: "above the loop, and revised by it: consequence updates the model and may update the purpose"
  leverage: "human + AI + tools, after principal choice or authorization, never before"

meta_loop:
  question: "did the protocol itself fail?"
  checks:
    - context_lost
    - wrong_question_chosen
    - uncertainty_hidden
    - authority_misunderstood
    - recurring_workflow_inefficient
    - tool_failed
    - representation_misled
    - principal_carried_what_the_system_should_have
  steps: [preserve_failure, propose_improvement, implement_within_bounded_scope, independent_evaluation, did_later_cases_improve, retain_or_revert]
  status: "the most defensible form of recursive self-improvement available to this protocol today; improvement is toward what, according to whom, with what evidence, under whose authority"

coupled_system:
  claim: >
    the useful unit may be the principal + durable externalized cognition +
    frontier intelligence + specialized agents + tools + reality feedback +
    recursive process improvement, whose shared state survives conversations
    and model generations.
  status: inferred, not established
  standard: >
    externalized structure counts as cognitive leverage only when it changes
    what the principal can practically do (a contradiction noticed, a prior
    insight resurfaced, a constraint that follows work into a child, an
    inquiry an agent can continue, a question visible where its answer changes
    the next action); a large graph is not the measure.

fear:
  reference_condition: "not the absence of fear; less prevention of values-consistent, reality-testing movement while fear's information is preserved"
  loop: [fear_exists, what_is_it_predicting, what_is_the_evidence, what_is_genuinely_protected, smallest_reversible_move, what_happens, update]

reported_experience_rule:
  rule: >
    an experience of meaning, convergence, or coincidence enters as an
    observation before any explanation; interpretations are listed as
    alternatives with evidence and an open question; the record neither
    confirms a destiny nor dismisses the experience.
  statuses: [reported, observed, inferred, assumed, predicted, disputed, unknown]

next_slice:
  question: >
    Can the principal enter anything, and within one continuous Yawn
    experience, watch it become an attributed, revisable orientation that
    helps them discover what matters, find the most consequential unanswered
    question, and add governed AI leverage to the next warranted turn?
  criterion:
    - one natural expression with mixed feeling, purpose, uncertainty, relationship, claim, question, and possible action
    - source preserved exactly
    - provisional decomposition with the existing ontology; place in the holarchy found without the principal categorizing
    - the smallest recognizable orientation exposed
    - the one question most likely to alter a rightful next turn surfaced, with why it was chosen inspectable
    - correction of any inferred relationship or purpose, visibly changing the question, model, or movement frontier
    - an authorized child inquiry carried by a research or execution agent
    - result, consequence, and proof preserved
    - state restored on return without reconstruction
    - one failure of the process becoming a bounded improvement that improves a later case
    - no new ontology unless the existing contracts are proven insufficient by this run
  relation: "the same slice as docs/execution-plans/theory-carries-builder-run-01-v0.3.md's first-minute Yawn, and Run 01 Lap 1"

boundary: >
  This record grants nothing and ranks nothing. It is checkable against the
  governing sources and against the product (yawn.bot
  src/domain/yawn-agency-interface.ts mirrors its lists and comparator). Only
  the principal accepts it as the protocol's statement of purpose.
